{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,9]],"date-time":"2026-09-09T13:28:28Z","timestamp":1788960508323,"version":"build-2803163510"},"reference-count":62,"publisher":"Wiley","issue":"23","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2024,7,31]],"date-time":"2024-07-31T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1722384000000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by-nc\/4.0\/"}],"funder":[{"DOI":"10.13039\/100014440","name":"Ministerio de Ciencia, Innovaci\u00f3n y Universidades","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["PID2021-127957NB-I00"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["PID2021-127957NB-I00"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/100014440","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/100014440","name":"Ministerio de Ciencia, Innovaci\u00f3n y Universidades","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["TED2021-132550B-C21"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["TED2021-132550B-C21"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/100014440","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/100010434","name":"'la Caixa' Foundation","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["LCF\/BQ\/DI22\/11940040"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["LCF\/BQ\/DI22\/11940040"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/100010434","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100003086","name":"Eusko Jaurlaritza","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["IT1453-22"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["IT1453-22"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100003086","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":["chemistry-europe.onlinelibrary.wiley.com"],"crossmark-restriction":true},"short-container-title":["ChemSusChem"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024,12,6]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title><jats:p>Electrocatalysis holds the key to the decentralized production of hydrogen peroxide <jats:italic>via<\/jats:italic> the two\u2010electron oxygen reduction reaction (ORR, O<jats:sub>2(g)<\/jats:sub>+2H<jats:sup>+<\/jats:sup>+2e<jats:sup>\u2212<\/jats:sup>\u2010&gt;H<jats:sub>2<\/jats:sub>O<jats:sub>2(aq)<\/jats:sub>). However, cost\u2010effective, active, and selective catalysts are still sought after. While density functional theory (DFT) has already led to the discovery of various enhanced catalysts, it has a severe yet often unnoticed drawback: the ill description of O<jats:sub>2<\/jats:sub> and H<jats:sub>2<\/jats:sub>O<jats:sub>2<\/jats:sub>. Here, we analyze the impact of the errors in those two species on the most widespread activity plots in the literature, namely free\u2010energy diagrams and Sabatier\u2010type volcano plots. Uncorrected or partially corrected gas\u2010phase energies lead to appreciably different activity plots that may provide inaccurate predictions. Indeed, we show for a variety of electrocatalysts that only when the errors in O<jats:sub>2<\/jats:sub> and H<jats:sub>2<\/jats:sub>O<jats:sub>2<\/jats:sub> are corrected can DFT mimic the experiments. In sum, this work provides concrete guidelines to avoid a common pitfall of computational models for electrocatalytic hydrogen peroxide production.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1002\/cssc.202400873","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2024,6,18]],"date-time":"2024-06-18T12:33:47Z","timestamp":1718714027000},"update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1002\/crossmark_policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":12,"title":["Error Awareness in the Volcano Plots of Oxygen Electroreduction to Hydrogen Peroxide"],"prefix":"10.1002","volume":"17","author":[{"given":"Ricardo","family":"Urrego\u2010Ortiz","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Materials Science and Chemical Physics &amp; Institute of Theoretical and Computational Chemistry (IQTCUB) University of Barcelona  C\/Mart\u00ed i Franqu\u00e8s 1 08028 Barcelona Spain"},{"name":"Nano-Bio Spectroscopy Group and European Theoretical Spectroscopy Facility (ETSF) Department of Polymers and Advanced Materials: Physics, Chemistry and Technology University of the Basque Country UPV\/EHU  Av. Tolosa 72 20018 San Sebasti\u00e1n Spain"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Michell O.","family":"Almeida","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Pharmacy School of Pharmaceutical Sciences University of S\u00e3o Paulo  Av Prof Lineu Prestes 580, Building 13 S\u00e3o Paulo 05508-000 SP Brazil"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-5147-8635","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Federico","family":"Calle\u2010Vallejo","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Nano-Bio Spectroscopy Group and European Theoretical Spectroscopy Facility (ETSF) Department of Polymers and Advanced Materials: Physics, Chemistry and Technology University of the Basque Country UPV\/EHU  Av. Tolosa 72 20018 San Sebasti\u00e1n Spain"},{"name":"IKERBASQUE, Basque Foundation for Science  Plaza de Euskadi 5 48009 Bilbao Spain"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"311","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2024,7,31]]},"reference":[{"key":"e_1_2_13_1_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/j.jclepro.2015.03.015"},{"key":"e_1_2_13_2_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1007\/s11783-020-1293-2"},{"key":"e_1_2_13_3_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/j.jhazmat.2021.127068"},{"key":"e_1_2_13_4_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1038\/s41578-023-00564-y"},{"key":"e_1_2_13_5_1","unstructured":"S. Brueske C. Kramer A. Fisher \u201cBandwidth Study on Energy Use and Potential Energy Saving Opportunities in U.\u2005S. Chemical Manufacturing \u201d can be found underhttps:\/\/www.osti.gov\/biblio\/1248749 2015."},{"key":"e_1_2_13_6_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1021\/acscatal.8b00217"},{"key":"e_1_2_13_7_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/j.chemosphere.2019.03.042"},{"key":"e_1_2_13_8_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1